\node[below right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (axis cs:0,-2) {$(0,-2)$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Concave up since $k=\tfrac{1}{2}>0$; vertex $(0,-2)$.
$\tfrac{1}{2}x^2-2=0$
$x^2=4$
$x=\pm2$
Plot the vertex $(0,-2)$ and the $x$-intercepts $(-2,0)$ and $(2,0)$, then draw a concave-up parabola through them.

